    "question": {
      ":question/id": "54659204-796d-56af-8249-d35116a3ae36",
      ":question/problem": "Find the **exact** value of $\\cos\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that*\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi}{12}=\\frac{5\\pi}{4}-\\frac{4\\pi}{3}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos(x-y)=\\cos x\\cos y+\\sin x\\sin y.\n$$\n\nApply it to the decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)=\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}-\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\right).\n$$\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\right)+\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{4}\\right)\\sin\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{3}\\right)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the signed special-angle values and combine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&=\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right) \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{4} \\\\\n&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2} + \\sqrt{6}}{4}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
